    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1183">

                <pb facs="0971" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/5276.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-18T19:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 18, 1912—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On account of general excitement of people here over her supposed mission,
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs strongly urged me to request Department not to
                    allow <hi rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> to enter port of Vera Cruz for the
                    present. I replied that I would transmit his request.</p>
                <p>In view of my remonstrances there will be no bombardment ox city, but opposing
                    forces will engage outside.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
